# Agentic / implementation routing

**ADF status mirror: COMPLETE ADF-A–ADF-H; ADF-EX-17 DEFERRED VERIFICATION; FOUNDATION EXIT ACCEPTED; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A NEXT.**

**CKR status mirror: COMPLETE CKR-A–CKR-I; IN EXECUTION CKR-J; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A BLOCKED ON CKR EXIT.**

CKR-A–I are complete/accepted. CKR-J is in execution/routing-cutover validation. Product implementation remains blocked until CKR-K.

Primary shared authority remains root `AGENTS.md`, the CKR README/ownership inventory, and accepted ADF scope/security mechanics. All accepted semantic families through ARCH are canonicalized; Phase 001–010 sources are provenance.

For a known stable ID, use `python3 scripts/agentic/resolve_stable_id.py <ID>` to get the deterministic canonical locator. Use `--history` only for explicit provenance/history. For an unknown semantic location, use one bounded OKF route then the canonical owner.

Do not infer authority from OKF, resolver output alone, recency, search order, Git history, vendor skill, tool memory, source availability or path presence. CKR-J does not authorize CKR-K or implementation work.
